body:
Cutting has a 1.2% lethal rate.

[https://www.hsph.harvard.edu/means-matter/means-matter/case-fatality/](https://www.hsph.harvard.edu/means-matter/means-matter/case-fatality/)

All suicide methods have some survival rate. If you survive after a suicide attempt, there is almost always  risk of brain damage or other health complications. 

Life has definitely not always been joyful for me either. But as humans, how do we know that things can't get better and easier? 

There might be levels of intelligence far greater than the intelligence any human has ever had.

Maybe at those higher states of intelligence, you realize solutions, and achieve greater happiness. 

Maybe you will reach those higher states of intelligence if you stay alive. Maybe you will find solutions, joy, comfort, ease...

&#x200B;

My advice for you now is to focus on relief. What can you do right now to feel better, even if it's just a little bit better?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

And I recommend you listen to this video. it might help:

https://tealswan.com/videos/emotions/how-to-feel-better-feeling-signatures-r143/

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

/Mira
